      "summaryMarkdown": "F-S3-1 is resolved: the Release is now titled `v1.0.0`, and `git_release_name` covers future releases. Final review should confirm three things: the `build(release)` commit carries the key, the next Release-plz run on that push succeeds without a tag or release PR (a `build` commit does not match `release_commits`), and a later release gets a `vX.Y.Z` title. OWN-1: `RELEASE_PLZ_TOKEN` is the only secret (names only; updated 2026-10-18T23:02:16Z when the owner extended the PAT). OWN-2: \"Release tags\" is active on `refs/tags/v*` with `update`, `deletion`, `non_fast_forward` and no bypass. WF-1: `release-plz.yml` (84ebf2f) is RayX.CLI's workflow with this repository's guard, `ci.yml`'s `actions/checkout@v7`, `needs: release` on `release-pr` and a header that fits (release-plz creates the Release). `ci.yml` is unchanged since 7d55b99. FIRST-1: run 39171612775 (0c0357b) failed with 403 on `git/tags` (the PAT, the recorded t09 blocker); run 39174989504 (55ae9cc, which differs from 0c0357b only in `state.json`) succeeded and tagged `v1.0.0` (annotated, at 55ae9cc). The Release is not a draft or prerelease, and its body equals the `## [1.0.0] - 2026-10-18` section line for line. There is no per-crate tag, and no release-plz PR was ever opened. `ci.yml` passed for 340fac5, 0c0357b and 55ae9cc on Ubuntu and Windows. The Release came from the next push rather than a `workflow_dispatch` re-run, which is acceptable because the product content is identical. FIRST-2: the recorded `check-tag-consumer` passed, with `(proc-macro)` in the derive line.",
